  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Growth Research - Synthesis reports 2016</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Research and development activity contributing to the UK&#x2019;s strategy to address key development challenges.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The funders wish to commission a number of short (c 20 pages) reports, to include a stand-alone summary, which synthesise the emerging evidence from the programme to date. While it is essential that the reports are based on academically rigorous analysis, they will be aimed primarily at the policy community and other interested users and written in appropriately accessible language. The reports would be expected to:
&#x2022;	summarise emerging evidence from the DEGRP research conducted to date within a workable thematic organising  framework (see below);
&#x2022;	set this evidence in the context of the existing research landscape, identifying, for example, where established findings are confirmed or challenged by new research;
&#x2022;	highlight the resulting implications for policy and, where appropriate, for the future research agenda in the relevant area.</narrative>
  </description>
